 "asked_at": "2026-10-18T00:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**I’d suggest she skip her outdoor morning walk today, Sunday, October 18, and walk indoors instead.** Singapore’s National Environment Agency forecasts the haze-related air-quality index at **150–220 (Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy)** today and advises older adults to **minimise outdoor activity**. If she has chronic heart or lung disease, the advice is to **avoid outdoor activity**. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-17-october-2026?utm_source=openai))\n\nThe forecast cannot tell us exactly what the air will be like on her route in the morning. Before any necessary trip outside, check the **1-hour PM₂.₅ reading** for her area in the myENV app or on Singapore’s haze site. If it is **High**, NEA advises older adults to avoid all outdoor activity for the next hour. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-17-october-2026?utm_source=openai))",
